WEBVTT

00:00:13.304 --> 00:00:15.223
Seriously? Three bronze coins?

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.893
This ain't enough pay
for all the hauling we did!

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:27.068
What am I supposed to do
with a half-dead orc?

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:29.779
Wait until you hear him talk!

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.781
Plenty of other shops might want him.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:32.991
Damn him.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.536
I found a scouring pad along the way.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.872
How much can you give us for this?

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:41.416
A filthy piece of trash.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:50.383
120 bronze pieces.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:54.846
Two whole figures more!

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:57.557
Uncle is dirt-cheap!

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.271
UNCLE:
YOU'RE FINE THE WAY YOU ARE

00:02:16.511 --> 00:02:18.179
GET HOME

00:02:23.393 --> 00:02:24.435
SOLD CHEAPER THAN A SCOURING PAD

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.821
I'm worth less than a scouring pad?

00:02:34.904 --> 00:02:37.073
How do you not know that, Uncle?

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:46.624
Why do you two have nosebleeds?

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:54.173
I know.
I must have used the memory erase spell.

00:02:54.757 --> 00:02:56.759
My memories flooded back just now.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:57.886
Mine too.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.763
I recalled reading the page about this

00:03:01.764 --> 00:03:03.391
right now.

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:12.734
Fujimiya,
read the first page of my notebook.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.445
What a tattered notebook.

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:17.906
Don't read past the first page!

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.454
"Sold cheaper than a scouring pad."

00:03:26.122 --> 00:03:30.168
I got rid of this tragic memory
once I learned the memory erase spell.

00:03:30.668 --> 00:03:34.255
This must've been quite a shock,
even for you, Uncle.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:38.968
When there's a reminder,
erased memories can come back.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.347
The nosebleed is a sign of warning

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.683
by the spirit of memory
that you're about to have a flashback.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:49.020
But we watched the actual event,
so what can we do?

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:52.440
Isn't there a better way
to heed a warning?

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:54.400
Are you all good?

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:55.902
I've had enough.

00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:57.362
My shoulders are sore.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.698
So what becomes of Uncle?

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:30.979
So they threw me into the basement
of a freak show.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:33.856
I'm skipping a week.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.608
Why's that?

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:39.821
The shopkeeper completely forgot about me.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:47.287
Without the puddle from the rain
on the third day, I would've been dead.

00:04:49.163 --> 00:04:52.583
A single ray of light
cuts through darkness.

00:04:53.084 --> 00:04:55.044
Just like Voltteccer.

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:56.546
Bet you didn't know this.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:59.340
There's a game on Mega Drive
called Pulseman.

00:04:59.424 --> 00:05:02.677
His ultimate move is supposed to be
pronounced with strength.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.387
It's pronounced "Voltteccer"!

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:07.765
When bouncing off walls, he can
stay in his Voltteccer state indefinitely.

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:10.351
It's a powerful and beautiful move.

00:05:10.435 --> 00:05:14.147
You can't talk about Pulseman and
not mention the semi-transparent levels.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.064
He's lost it.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.774
A beautiful expression
of the electricity world.

00:05:16.858 --> 00:05:19.944
-Look at what Uncle's become.
-No, you got it wrong.

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:23.823
I was speaking to the ray of moonlight
to try to remain sane.

00:05:23.906 --> 00:05:25.700
Can't you tell from the look on my face?

00:05:25.783 --> 00:05:27.952
I knew what I was doing.

00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:31.372
Talk about being ahead of its time.
The team that developed Pulseman…

00:05:31.456 --> 00:05:32.457
I-I can see that.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.208
…hit a jackpot with a game called Pokemon.

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:35.585
You're right.

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:40.923
But I know that someday, they'll release
Pulseman 2 on a SEGA console.

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:45.178
Pulseman becomes invincible
while in Voltteccer mode.

00:05:45.261 --> 00:05:48.598
It's just the coolest move ever.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.811
He shines beautifully,
like this ray of moonlight.

00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:55.688
An invincible body.

00:05:56.898 --> 00:05:59.650
What? You're thanking me?

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.778
I'm not just saying it.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:04.155
I don't grovel, you know.

00:06:04.655 --> 00:06:07.408
You are the most beautiful thing
I've seen in this world.

00:06:11.412 --> 00:06:13.790
Who's there?

00:06:16.584 --> 00:06:19.253
Could this ray of light be sentient?

00:06:21.839 --> 00:06:24.717
You are the spirit of light, Kilighd.

00:06:26.844 --> 00:06:28.054
Chant…

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:30.890
the ancient words?

00:06:34.018 --> 00:06:37.230
Kilighd l'gid riolran.

00:06:45.863 --> 00:06:47.281
A sword of light.

00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:50.034
That was the very first magic I used.

00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:51.869
I got out thanks to this spell.

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:59.669
Uncle, don't tell me
you were muttering at--

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:02.255
Yes, that was the spirit of light.

00:07:02.338 --> 00:07:05.591
There are others like the spirit of wind
and fire and whatnot.

00:07:05.675 --> 00:07:08.427
How did you suddenly gain the ability
to converse with spirits?

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.973
-Is this his translation ability?
-Yes.

00:07:12.557 --> 00:07:16.894
Was Uncle using the translation ability
given by the gods?

00:07:18.563 --> 00:07:19.772
Yes,

00:07:19.856 --> 00:07:23.401
that must be the secret behind
Uncle's exceptional magical talent.

00:07:24.735 --> 00:07:26.654
Even back in the Shielded City,

00:07:26.737 --> 00:07:30.658
Uncle was the only one
who could communicate with the spirits!

00:07:33.661 --> 00:07:35.246
So that's what it was.

00:07:35.746 --> 00:07:40.042
I was wondering why my take on magic
differed from others'.

00:07:42.336 --> 00:07:47.341
Had I communicated with the residents,
I could've known this while I was there.

00:07:47.425 --> 00:07:49.635
Actually,

00:07:49.719 --> 00:07:54.182
how did you explain your sudden
magic and language acquisition?

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:58.019
Well, you know,

00:07:59.103 --> 00:08:02.273
I can pick up video games
even when I have no idea

00:08:02.356 --> 00:08:04.775
what the in-game English means.

00:08:04.859 --> 00:08:09.739
I thought my adaptability
honed from video games was at work.

00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:11.991
You don't have that kind of talent.

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:15.077
His trust in video games
never fails to amuse.

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:17.997
So then what happened?

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.081
Oh, right.

00:08:19.582 --> 00:08:22.793
I used the Sword of Light
and escaped the cell.

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:31.469
I also freed the little creatures
in captivity on my way out.

00:08:37.475 --> 00:08:39.227
How cute!

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:42.021
They liked you! Did you keep them as pets?

00:08:43.731 --> 00:08:44.732
Well, no.

00:08:46.317 --> 00:08:48.694
One of them nipped my carotid artery.

00:08:48.778 --> 00:08:50.154
Ferocious monsters!

00:09:02.333 --> 00:09:04.001
Help me!

00:09:04.085 --> 00:09:05.920
What in the world is happening?

00:09:06.003 --> 00:09:08.714
Malicious rodents, death beasts,
and crazed-fanged fowls!

00:09:08.798 --> 00:09:12.426
Monsters from across the Eastern continent
have broken free!

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.222
Someone help!

00:09:29.318 --> 00:09:31.696
W-Will I

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:35.658
live as an ordinary commoner

00:09:36.158 --> 00:09:38.911
who runs for his life?

00:09:39.996 --> 00:09:41.747
Or, will I…

00:09:45.585 --> 00:09:48.588
Regsuuid zaldohna!

00:09:57.805 --> 00:09:59.682
Thank you so much. You saved me--

00:10:00.349 --> 00:10:03.394
You've done well.

00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:09.108
You are safe now, rest assured.

00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:11.068
Transfer the injured, Spirit.

00:10:11.152 --> 00:10:12.320
Destination set.

00:10:30.296 --> 00:10:33.883
So I fought throughout the night.

00:10:38.346 --> 00:10:40.973
The battle finally ended at last.

00:10:45.478 --> 00:10:46.812
Baraib garl.

00:11:00.743 --> 00:11:05.665
Many thanks to the monsters
that nourished my starved body.

00:11:08.876 --> 00:11:10.753
How do I say this,

00:11:11.337 --> 00:11:15.466
though my 17 years in Another World
was nothing but hardship

00:11:15.549 --> 00:11:20.137
as you saw, at least I had a great start.

00:11:20.638 --> 00:11:21.722
Is he being serious?

00:11:21.806 --> 00:11:24.141
How is this a great start?

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:29.146
Had I been appraised for more than
a scouring pad, I'd have no complaints.

00:11:33.401 --> 00:11:35.778
I'm sorry.

00:11:35.861 --> 00:11:38.197
It's late, I have to get going.

00:11:39.073 --> 00:11:41.158
I can't miss out on fried chicken.

00:11:41.742 --> 00:11:43.702
Let's watch the rest on another day.

00:11:44.203 --> 00:11:45.496
Good idea.

00:11:45.579 --> 00:11:48.833
It only went downhill from here anyway.

00:11:50.918 --> 00:11:52.586
Things got even worse?

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:55.673
What do you mean? What happened?

00:11:56.841 --> 00:11:58.634
Nothing, really.

00:11:59.718 --> 00:12:02.054
I saved Elf from a dragon.

00:12:03.472 --> 00:12:07.476
She thanked me by berating me.
What a pain.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.228
This part is crucial!

00:12:09.311 --> 00:12:11.480
This is the part I came for!

00:12:15.192 --> 00:12:18.112
Start dinner without me. Okay.

00:12:18.863 --> 00:12:22.575
Now, show me some action worth giving up
my fried chicken for, Uncle!

00:12:22.658 --> 00:12:24.660
All right, watch closely.

00:12:25.286 --> 00:12:28.914
The battle against a Venom Dragon happened
on my 9th day in Another World.

00:12:29.957 --> 00:12:31.417
It went like this.

00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:38.215
Ta-da, I won.

00:12:38.799 --> 00:12:40.134
The fight ended!

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:42.720
My fried chicken.

00:12:42.803 --> 00:12:46.015
Your magic is unmatched!
You struck down a dragon in one go!

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.728
I couldn't have slayed it that easily
under normal conditions.

00:12:50.811 --> 00:12:52.188
But see,

00:12:53.481 --> 00:12:57.526
Elf had already dealt repeated blows
on this part of its body.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:00.029
So I went for this vulnerable spot.

00:13:00.613 --> 00:13:04.200
She almost got the whole thing by herself.

00:13:13.542 --> 00:13:14.752
An orc.

00:13:21.884 --> 00:13:24.261
I didn't see anything.

00:13:24.345 --> 00:13:26.722
Also, I'm not an orc.

00:13:28.349 --> 00:13:29.600
Are you covered?

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.978
Do you know how to zip it up?

00:13:39.568 --> 00:13:42.446
I owe you my gratitude, swordsman.

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:48.035
Anyone else would've done the same.

00:13:55.543 --> 00:13:57.044
What a monstrosity.

00:13:58.045 --> 00:14:01.048
You must be an evil orc.

00:14:01.549 --> 00:14:02.591
How ugly.

00:14:02.675 --> 00:14:05.970
Your ugliness is unforgivable.

00:14:06.053 --> 00:14:07.763
She glitched.

00:14:08.305 --> 00:14:10.724
She became unhinged.

00:14:10.808 --> 00:14:12.893
Where'd you get that knife?

00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:15.437
W-What am I doing?

00:14:16.063 --> 00:14:17.565
Pardon me.

00:14:18.148 --> 00:14:19.525
You stabbed yourself!

00:14:19.608 --> 00:14:20.818
Are you hurt?

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.828
H-Hey!

00:14:30.911 --> 00:14:31.912
What are you doing?

00:14:31.996 --> 00:14:33.622
Where's the wound?
We have to stop the bleeding!

00:14:33.706 --> 00:14:36.417
I didn't get stabbed! I'm unharmed!

00:14:39.336 --> 00:14:40.754
There's not a single cut.

00:14:40.838 --> 00:14:42.590
Your skin is very smooth.

00:14:42.673 --> 00:14:44.592
Maybe the cut is somewhere else.

00:14:44.675 --> 00:14:46.635
What about here? Or here?

00:14:48.304 --> 00:14:49.638
Hey!

00:14:51.307 --> 00:14:53.100
You'll pay for this!

00:14:53.684 --> 00:14:57.396
My eyes will never forget your swine face!

00:14:58.522 --> 00:15:00.774
I'll make sure we're even someday!

00:15:01.358 --> 00:15:03.068
Are you sure you aren't hurt?

00:15:03.152 --> 00:15:06.113
Don't come any closer, you pervert orc!

00:15:06.196 --> 00:15:07.448
Pig, you are a pig!

00:15:07.531 --> 00:15:09.617
You pig, you ugly orc!

00:15:12.328 --> 00:15:15.205
Uncle, say something.

00:15:15.289 --> 00:15:21.086
No. Talking back in this situation
would only provoke her.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:22.671
Patience is key.

00:15:23.172 --> 00:15:26.508
What kind of student life did Uncle have?

00:15:27.718 --> 00:15:29.511
And this is when

00:15:30.638 --> 00:15:33.223
her pestering started.

00:15:34.808 --> 00:15:38.312
She stole my jacket and said
terrible things to me whenever I saw her.

00:15:38.395 --> 00:15:41.357
She didn't help me
when I got frozen in ice, too.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.566
Elf, that jerk.

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:45.319
Speaking of getting frozen in ice.

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:48.072
What happened after that night?

00:15:49.782 --> 00:15:52.242
Let me show you.

00:15:53.911 --> 00:15:55.704
My body feels heavy.

00:15:55.788 --> 00:15:58.332
Is this the aftermath
of getting stuck in ice?

00:16:01.251 --> 00:16:03.629
What is this soft thing on my body?

00:16:18.268 --> 00:16:20.396
What are you doing in my room?

00:16:20.479 --> 00:16:24.650
Some tribes in the North
use their preys' organs to stay warm.

00:16:24.733 --> 00:16:27.611
It's chilly, so I was warming up!

00:16:27.695 --> 00:16:28.737
That's a stretch.

00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:30.864
What a terrible excuse.

00:16:31.448 --> 00:16:33.283
That makes sense.

00:16:33.367 --> 00:16:34.910
-He believed her!
-I don't believe this!

00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:37.496
Yes, it's a bit chilly tonight.

00:16:37.579 --> 00:16:40.499
Let's sleep in so we don't catch a cold.

00:16:40.582 --> 00:16:43.752
It's cold, so I'll warm up with your body.

00:16:44.461 --> 00:16:47.589
Using me like an organ from a hunt.

00:16:50.718 --> 00:16:52.052
Do as you please.

00:16:57.599 --> 00:16:59.268
What's with you?

00:17:03.522 --> 00:17:04.648
Mother.

00:17:05.357 --> 00:17:06.567
Mother.

00:17:07.317 --> 00:17:08.318
No.

00:17:09.737 --> 00:17:10.738
Mother.

00:17:11.905 --> 00:17:13.365
Mother.

00:17:16.952 --> 00:17:18.245
Are you--

00:17:18.328 --> 00:17:21.290
I don't want to work!

00:17:21.373 --> 00:17:23.375
You told me, Mother.

00:17:24.001 --> 00:17:25.294
"Life is a piece of cake."

00:17:25.377 --> 00:17:30.007
I'd never go hungry
as long as I have the god-freezing sword.

00:17:30.591 --> 00:17:33.886
I don't want to work, Mother.

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:38.974
Mother, you left with a younger man
when I was nine.

00:17:46.148 --> 00:17:47.566
Why'd you hit me?

00:17:47.649 --> 00:17:51.445
I couldn't bear to watch you complain
about wanting to be a bum.

00:17:51.528 --> 00:17:54.198
I'm kidding.

00:17:54.281 --> 00:17:57.493
I, Mabel, want to find work!

00:17:58.577 --> 00:18:01.288
It's noble to work!

00:18:01.371 --> 00:18:02.956
Your body says otherwise!

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:07.628
Like I said, sell that ring
and you don't have to earn a living.

00:18:07.711 --> 00:18:10.506
He's right, sell it off already.

00:18:13.092 --> 00:18:15.219
But I should be able to support myself.

00:18:15.302 --> 00:18:17.513
Working is for cattle.

00:18:18.097 --> 00:18:20.891
I don't understand how pawning works.

00:18:20.974 --> 00:18:22.643
I'll pitch a high price for you.

00:18:26.188 --> 00:18:30.609
This is my last resort,
I'll save it until I'm out of options.

00:18:31.193 --> 00:18:34.071
Oh, I see, okay.

00:18:34.655 --> 00:18:38.283
What if you were under Elf's care for now?

00:18:38.367 --> 00:18:39.368
What?

00:18:39.451 --> 00:18:41.495
You have money left over
from selling your ring.

00:18:42.287 --> 00:18:45.082
I deposited the money at the bank, but--

00:18:47.918 --> 00:18:49.128
Be my master!

00:18:51.255 --> 00:18:53.215
-Master!
-What?

00:18:56.301 --> 00:18:58.220
I-It's nothing.

00:18:58.303 --> 00:19:00.931
Don't say that
if you're going to be ashamed about it.

00:19:01.515 --> 00:19:05.227
Anyway, let's grab breakfast.

00:19:05.811 --> 00:19:07.354
I'll treat you two today.

00:19:08.147 --> 00:19:09.148
Bark!

00:19:15.487 --> 00:19:18.282
I haven't introduced myself yet.

00:19:18.991 --> 00:19:21.451
I am Mabel Rayveil.

00:19:21.994 --> 00:19:26.206
I'm the last of the Ice clan,
and my dream is to become an explorer.

00:19:26.707 --> 00:19:28.000
Great to meet you two.

00:19:28.625 --> 00:19:29.626
I am--

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.337
No, Elf will do.

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:36.008
I'm the only one of my kind
outside the kingdom's borders anyway.

00:19:36.884 --> 00:19:40.304
My mission is to find and gather
the scattered ancient relics.

00:19:40.804 --> 00:19:42.181
Good to be with both of you.

00:19:43.056 --> 00:19:44.433
I am Wolfgunblood.

00:19:44.516 --> 00:19:47.186
-Liar!
-He went for a fancy name!

00:19:47.769 --> 00:19:51.231
I'm traveling to find the way back
to my home country.

00:19:51.315 --> 00:19:52.357
Good to be with you both.

00:19:52.858 --> 00:19:54.651
Why'd you choose an alias?

00:19:55.235 --> 00:19:58.906
Don't tell your real name
to a bunch of strangers.

00:19:58.989 --> 00:20:01.658
He's known Elf
for at least three years by this point.

00:20:01.742 --> 00:20:03.994
He's well-versed
in parallel world customs.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:08.081
I am departing for Ikoza City now.

00:20:08.165 --> 00:20:11.710
Ikoza?
Isn't that where you sold your ring off?

00:20:11.793 --> 00:20:14.755
I don't recall
there being dungeons in that area.

00:20:15.505 --> 00:20:18.383
S-Shut it! Let me do as I please!

00:20:18.467 --> 00:20:19.927
Dummy! Womanizer orc!

00:20:20.677 --> 00:20:22.554
She wants to go buy her ring back.

00:20:22.638 --> 00:20:25.307
She feels threatened
by Mabel's appearance.

00:20:25.891 --> 00:20:27.476
Wolfgunblood.

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:28.685
Where is he?

00:20:31.063 --> 00:20:32.397
Wait, that's me.

00:20:32.481 --> 00:20:35.108
What will you be doing today?

00:20:35.192 --> 00:20:38.362
A hero is trying to clear
a dungeon nearby.

00:20:38.946 --> 00:20:40.322
I'll go scout it out.

00:20:41.198 --> 00:20:42.866
A hero of legendary strength.

00:20:44.284 --> 00:20:46.995
That title was vacant for 50 years
until her appointment.

00:20:47.621 --> 00:20:51.416
I heard she single-handedly slayed

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:55.337
a horde of legion-class beasts,
earning her the title "Shining Crusader".

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:57.839
Is that what happened? That's amazing!

00:20:57.923 --> 00:20:59.800
I will go with you, Wolf.

00:21:01.593 --> 00:21:06.348
But I'm a night owl.
I'll take a nap until around 2:00 p.m.

00:21:06.932 --> 00:21:09.935
So please stick around
until five o'clock or so.

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.442
And that's a wrap for the day.

00:21:17.526 --> 00:21:19.736
The party disbanded!

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:22.823
Mabel is a bum to the bone.
She can't join Uncle!

00:21:24.449 --> 00:21:27.619
Speaking of five o'clock,
look at the time.

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:29.997
Let's let Fujimiya get home.

00:21:32.499 --> 00:21:34.960
I should've gone with fried chicken.

00:21:35.043 --> 00:21:36.795
Are you starved?

00:21:38.505 --> 00:21:41.842
Wanna go eat some ramen?
I'll cover your tab.

00:21:42.968 --> 00:21:45.262
-You will?
-Are you sure, Uncle?

00:21:48.307 --> 00:21:49.308
No take-backs.

00:21:53.979 --> 00:21:57.065
Generally speaking,
Uncle's life in Another World was hellish.

00:21:58.817 --> 00:22:01.695
Though the gods of Another World
were quite shabby,

00:22:01.778 --> 00:22:03.947
at least Tsundere Elf and Mabel
were with Uncle.

00:22:05.615 --> 00:22:07.659
The bowl of ramen from my uncle

00:22:08.744 --> 00:22:10.245
was very tasty.

00:22:14.958 --> 00:22:18.795
He was a little short on money,
so Fujimiya spotted the rest.

00:23:45.924 --> 00:23:50.929
Subtitle translation by:
Megumi Hunter
